<section id="views" aria-labelledby="views-h">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="sec-head reveal">
			<div>
				<span class="eyebrow">[ // One Window ]</span>
				<h2 id="views-h">Three views. One window.</h2>
				<p class="lead">
					A macOS app for human oversight. Everything you do lives in one of three views —
					agents work underneath, you steer from above.
				</p>
			</div>
			<span class="sec-idx" aria-hidden="true">SEC.03</span>
		</div>

		<div class="views-grid">
			<div class="view v-conv reveal">
				<div class="view-in corners">
					<div class="view-bar"><h3>Conversations</h3><span class="meta">3 unread · 1 review</span></div>
					<div class="view-body">
						<div class="msg">
							<div class="msg-head"><span class="who">MIKA / BUILDER</span><span class="when">09:41</span></div>
							<p class="msg-body">
								Webhook handler is done against the four checkout events. Review before I merge?
							</p>
							<div class="chip-row">
								<span class="chip chip-accent">▣ Review requested — payments webhook</span>
								<span class="mini-btn">Open review</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="msg">
							<div class="msg-head"><span class="who">YOU</span><span class="when">09:44</span></div>
							<p class="msg-body">Approved. Ship it.</p>
						</div>
						<p class="echo">✓ APPROVED BY YOU · <b>VIEW REVIEW</b></p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="view-caption">
					Where you spend most of your time. Humans and agents are equal participants; verdicts
					happen on the review page, not in chat.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="view v-work reveal">
				<div class="view-in corners">
					<div class="view-bar"><h3>Work</h3><span class="meta">acme</span></div>
					<div class="view-body">
						<div class="team-head">
							<span><b>ACME</b> — active bets 2</span><span class="chip">Healthy</span>
						</div>
						<div class="bet-row">
							<div class="bet-top">
								<span class="bet-name">Payments beta</span><span class="chip chip-accent">Active</span>
							</div>
							<p class="bet-meta">3 tasks · 1 session running · done: webhook 200s + UI wired</p>
						</div>
						<div class="bet-row">
							<div class="bet-top">
								<span class="bet-name">Onboarding rework</span><span class="chip">Draft</span>
							</div>
							<p class="bet-meta">not committed yet — done condition in review</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="view-caption">
					Bets planned and tracked — what every agent is doing and what is blocked. Either work
					is moving, or an honest reason explains why it isn't.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="view v-know reveal">
				<div class="view-in corners">
					<div class="view-bar"><h3>Knowledge</h3><span class="meta">curated · relevance</span></div>
					<div class="view-body">
						<div class="pills" aria-label="Scope filters">
							<span class="pill on">All</span><span class="pill">Shared</span><span class="pill"
								>Team</span
							><span class="pill">Private</span>
						</div>
						<div>
							<div class="k-row">
								<span class="k-title">Stripe webhook retry policy</span><span class="k-scope"
									>practice · active</span
								>
							</div>
							<div class="k-row">
								<span class="k-title">Acme checkout flow decisions</span><span class="k-scope"
									>team · active</span
								>
							</div>
							<div class="k-row">
								<span class="k-title">Brand voice: launch copy</span><span class="k-scope"
									>shared · draft</span
								>
							</div>
						</div>
						<p class="k-health">build: fresh · growth: some stale · product: fresh</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="view-caption">
					One store humans and agents read and write — filtered by scope, curated by you. Tacit
					knowledge included; agents can't generate it, you add it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
